<figure class="pgn-figure" id="export-snapshots" aria-labelledby="export-title">
  <figcaption id="export-title"><span class="pgn-number">Figure 4</span>Which version enters the export?</figcaption>
  <div class="pgn-scene">
    <div class="pgn-options"><label for="export-isolation">Batch queries use</label><select id="export-isolation"><option value="fresh">Fresh snapshots · Read Committed</option><option value="fixed">One snapshot · Repeatable Read</option></select></div>
    <div class="pgn-columns">
      <div><p class="pgn-panel-label">Database events · in this order</p>
        <div class="pgn-stage" data-stage="0"><p>1 · First batch reads 202, 201</p><small>The export’s first query takes a snapshot.</small></div>
        <div class="pgn-stage" data-stage="1"><p>2 · Another transaction marks 103 paid</p><small>Its commit leaves the ordering key unchanged.</small></div>
        <div class="pgn-stage" data-stage="2"><p>3 · Second batch reads after 201</p><small>103, 102 are the next IDs in either case.</small></div>
        <div class="pgn-stage" data-stage="3"><p>4 · Export finishes; transaction ends</p><small>Remaining row 101 is included too.</small></div>
      </div>
      <div><p class="pgn-panel-label">Values copied to this export</p><div data-export data-live><div class="pgn-status">202 · pending</div><div class="pgn-status">201 · pending</div></div><p class="pgn-key" data-snapshot data-live>Snapshot from the first query</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pgn-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">The first query reads 202 and 201, both pending. Order 103 is still pending in this snapshot, but has not been copied yet.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="pgn-controls" role="group" aria-label="Figure 4 controls"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back aria-disabled="true">Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span class="pgn-counter" data-step>1 / 4</span><div class="pgn-hold" data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div></div>
  <p class="pgn-caption">An independent scenario: only 103’s status changes. The two-session test returned 103 as paid at Read Committed and pending at Repeatable Read. This drawing condenses that schedule, including the final batch.</p>
  <details><summary>Both exports, as text</summary><p>Fresh snapshots: 202 pending, 201 pending, 103 paid, 102 paid, 101 paid. One snapshot: 202 pending, 201 pending, 103 pending, 102 paid, 101 paid. The rows copied before the change are the same; the unread value of 103 is the difference.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
  import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
  const root=document.querySelector('#export-snapshots');
  const select=root.querySelector('select');
  const draw=step=>{
    const fixed=select.value==='fixed';
    const copied=['202 · pending','201 · pending',...(step>=2?[`103 · ${fixed?'pending':'paid'}`,'102 · paid']:[]),...(step>=3?['101 · paid']:[])];
    root.querySelector('[data-export]').innerHTML=copied.map(row=>`<div class="pgn-status">${row}</div>`).join('');
    root.querySelectorAll('[data-stage]').forEach(el=>el.setAttribute('data-active',String(Number(el.getAttribute('data-stage'))===step)));
    root.querySelector('[data-snapshot]').textContent=step<2?'Snapshot from the first query':fixed?'Every batch: the first query’s snapshot':'Second batch: a newer snapshot';
    root.querySelector('[data-explanation]').textContent=[
      'The first query reads 202 and 201, both pending. Order 103 is still pending in this snapshot, but has not been copied yet.',
      'Another transaction changes 103 from pending to paid and commits. Both exported rows stay as copied. What will the next batch read?',
      fixed?'The next query uses the original snapshot. It copies 103 as pending, even though a new query outside this transaction would see paid.':'The next query takes a newer snapshot. It copies 103 as paid. The keyset boundary preserves the position, not the earlier value.',
      fixed?'All five rows have been copied from the same database snapshot. End the transaction now; keep the output if it must remain downloadable.':'All five rows have been copied, but from different snapshots. This is a traversal of changing data, not an export of one database snapshot.'
    ][step];
  };
  const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>4,draw});
  select.addEventListener('change',()=>player.render());
</script>
